# One repo, three components, three sets of rules merged. Two of the rules the
# source repos carried were rewritten rather than copied; both are called out
# where they appear.

# --- macOS ----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store

# --- Xcode and xcodegen ---------------------------------------------------
# The project file is generated: `name:` in mac/project.yml decides what it is
# called, so ignore the shape rather than one filename.
*.xcodeproj/
DerivedData/
build/
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
scratch/

# --- Python ---------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- Secrets --------------------------------------------------------------
# .env and the copies a careless `cp` leaves next to it. The bare `.env` rule
# does not cover `.env.bak`, and one `git add -A` is all it takes. The
# negation is what keeps collector/.env.example tracked: it carries variable
# names, never values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*.token

# secrets/ holds the model provider's key and the mailbox credentials. The
# example files are the only things under it that may be tracked.
#
# `**/secrets/*` and not `secrets/`, for two reasons: a pattern with a slash
# in it is anchored to this directory, so the bare form would miss
# mail/secrets/, and git does not descend into an ignored directory, so a
# directory rule would make the negation below unreachable.
**/secrets/*
!**/secrets/*.example

# --- Machine-local config -------------------------------------------------
# config.json carries LAN addresses and paths. config.example.json is the
# tracked one and these patterns cannot match it. The second line is for
# `config.json.before-discovery` and its friends, which the bare name misses.
config.json
config.json.*

# --- Runtime state --------------------------------------------------------
# Written by a component run in place rather than deployed to the Pi. None of
# these names exists in the tracked tree.
state/
public/
logs/
briefings/
heartbeat/
*.log

# The two deploy roots, in case CHARON_MAIL_BASE or CHAT_BASE is ever pointed
# at a directory inside this checkout. Live mail is other people's
# correspondence and belongs in no repository.
#
# Deliberately NOT the bare `mail/` and `messages/` rules the source repos
# carried. `mail/` is this repo's own component, and `messages/` would match
# `mac/Sources/Messages/` wherever git is configured to ignore case, which is
# the default on macOS. Either one silently un-tracks working code.
charon-mail/
halftone-chat/

# --- Rendered audio -------------------------------------------------------
# collector/canned/ ships the manifest and no audio on purpose: the manifest
# is the list of phrases, not a promise that the wavs exist. Delete this line
# if you want your own rendered shelf in git. (mac/Resources/Canned/ is
# tracked and is not affected by this rule.)
collector/canned/*.wav
